.TH DNSSEC-CHECK 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dnssec-check \- verify an rgbdns signed snapshot and signature lifetime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dnssec-check
.RI [ data.signed
.RI [ dnssec ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Accepts signed tinydns text or CDB data, structurally validates DNSSEC records,
cryptographically verifies every authoritative RRset, verifies the NSEC cycle,
and rejects signatures that are invalid or inside the configured refresh
window. One tab-separated status line is printed per zone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero only when every configured zone verifies; 100 for usage errors and 111
for verification or operational failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnssec-sign (1),
.BR dnssec-data (1),
.BR rgbdns (7)
